# TeacherAssist implementation summary discipline

Whenever you implement, fix, or materially change TeacherAssist behavior, **update `docs/teacher-assist/IMPLEMENTATION_SUMMARY.md` in the same pass**. Do not defer doc updates to a follow-up unless the user explicitly asks for code-only work.

## Required updates

For phase work or any substantive TeacherAssist change, the summary must reflect:

- What was added or changed (APIs, services, UI, migrations, config)
- Files touched (backend, frontend, tests)
- Tests run and validation performed
- Remaining gaps / known limitations affected
- Next recommended phase (when applicable)

Also keep aligned when relevant:

- `docs/teacher-assist/PHASE_STATUS.md`
- `docs/teacher-assist/KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md`

## Phase sections

New phases get a dedicated section in `IMPLEMENTATION_SUMMARY.md` following existing format:

- What was implemented
- Explicit non-goals preserved
- Backend / frontend files changed
- Tests added / run
- Manual validation checklist (for phases)
- Remaining gaps
- Next recommended phase

Update prior phase "next recommended phase" and stale limitation bullets so they do not contradict the new work.

## Scope

This applies to TeacherAssist changes across backend, frontend, worker, migrations, infrastructure under `infrastructure/aws/teacher-assist/`, and related tests/docs — not trading/Coinbase code unless the user explicitly includes it.

Reference: `docs/teacher-assist/IMPLEMENTATION_RULES.md`
